  "notes": "A common word in news, politics, and intellectual discussion. Can imply either fair critical evaluation or negative fault-finding, depending on context.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {厳|きび}しく{批判|ひはん}する: to harshly criticize\n- {批判|ひはん}を{受|う}ける: to receive criticism\n- {批判|ひはん}を{浴|あ}びる: to be showered with criticism\n- {批判|ひはん}{的|てき}: critical (adjective)\n- {批判|ひはん}{精神|せいしん}: critical spirit\n- {自己|じこ}{批判|ひはん}: self-criticism\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {非難|ひなん}する: to condemn, blame — stronger and more accusatory\n- {評論|ひょうろん}する: to review, comment — more neutral and analytical\n- {指摘|してき}する: to point out — neutral, factual identification of issues\n- {文句|もんく}を{言|い}う: to complain — informal, personal grievances",
